# Cloudflare Pages matches _redirects on the PATH only, not the host. Rules
# written as full URLs (https://www.example.com/*) are silently ignored here;
# that is a Netlify feature, not a Pages one. Three such rules sat in this file
# doing nothing and implying a www-to-apex redirect that never happened.
#
# All seven hosts therefore serve the document rather than redirecting. That is
# safe, and it is the same mechanism already chosen for the alias domains: the
# canonical is baked in at build and always names the primary, so search engines
# consolidate on one URL. Verified on every host.
#
# A real 301 from www to apex needs a zone-level Redirect Rule, one per zone,
# which needs an access level this token does not have. Worth doing when it is
# available: www-to-apex is the classic duplication case and a redirect handles
# it more decisively than a canonical hint.

# Path-based rules do work. The handoff's robots.txt advertised /sitemap.xml and
# Astro emits an index, so this keeps a published URL alive.
/sitemap.xml   /sitemap-index.xml   301
